WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.225 --> 00:00:03.450
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:04.788
- We didn't wanna leave you out.

00:00:04.788 --> 00:00:05.621
- Oh!

00:00:05.621 --> 00:00:07.740
- You're welcome. Welcome to the show.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:10.491
- Thank you. It's my
great pleasure to be here.

00:00:10.491 --> 00:00:12.510
"The Meddler." Okay so-

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:13.343
- The what?

00:00:13.343 --> 00:00:14.340
- We were in a movie together.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:15.791
- I was gonna say, do
y'all know each other?

00:00:15.791 --> 00:00:16.950
- We didn't have any scenes together.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.750
- Oh, that's so- that bums me out.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:20.137
I'd interview people all
the time, they're like,

00:00:20.137 --> 00:00:21.150
"Well, yeah, we were
in the movie together,

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:23.010
but we never saw each
other." Like, that's sad.

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:23.940
- I love that movie.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:24.773
- Yeah.

00:00:24.773 --> 00:00:26.310
- It was a great movie.
And I just met Tom Brady

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:27.600
last night, for the first time.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:28.433
- Oh really?

00:00:28.433 --> 00:00:29.858
- He's in the movie, "80 for Brady," but

00:00:29.858 --> 00:00:31.980
never met him while we were filming it,

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:33.390
but he's such a great guy.

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:34.223
- Wow.

00:00:34.223 --> 00:00:36.210
- Yeah, oh my god, that last- yeah the-

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:37.620
I don't wanna spoil it
for anybody but yeah,

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:38.670
the scene where he's talking a little,

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:40.080
he's talking about the
end. I was, like, crying.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:40.980
I was, like, "Wait,

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.898
why is Tom Brady making me cry right now?"

00:00:42.898 --> 00:00:43.731
(audience laughing)

00:00:43.731 --> 00:00:45.420
It happened. I was, like, "Okay,

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:46.470
he could pull some heartstrings."

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:47.995
How is your family doing?

00:00:47.995 --> 00:00:51.090
- Ah, thank you for asking.
My family is on fire.

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:51.923
- They are?

00:00:51.923 --> 00:00:54.810
- Yeah. My daughters,
my girls are, you know,

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:55.863
there they are. Okay so-

00:00:55.863 --> 00:00:58.630
- It's a shame no one's
attractive in your family.

00:00:58.630 --> 00:00:59.670
(audience laughing)

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:00.676
Oh my gosh.

00:01:00.676 --> 00:01:03.176
- Well, I married the right
D-N-A. What can I say?

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.670
- You got "Sexiest Man Alive!"

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:08.520
I think you're doing alright. (laughs)

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:09.353
I love what you said.

00:01:09.353 --> 00:01:10.560
(audience and Rose clapping)

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:12.360
Your wife, so she recently, um,

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:14.490
ended her run with "Real Housewives."

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:15.323
- She did.

00:01:15.323 --> 00:01:16.440
- Were you excited about that.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:19.663
- I am thrilled about
that. I get my wife back.

00:01:19.663 --> 00:01:20.850
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:23.220
So for fans of that show,
sorry she's not gonna be there,

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:24.373
but I get her back.

00:01:24.373 --> 00:01:25.206
(audience laughing)

00:01:25.206 --> 00:01:27.270
- That's awesome. What's
your favorite reality show.

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:28.103
You watch reality TV?

00:01:28.103 --> 00:01:29.430
- You know what? "Real Housewives."

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:30.263
- Really?

00:01:30.263 --> 00:01:31.096
- "Of Beverly Hills," yeah.

00:01:31.096 --> 00:01:33.030
That was the only one
I ever really got into.

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:35.340
It was so entertaining. Oh my goodness.

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:38.160
- Well, it's amazing, the
people who watch the show,

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:39.933
and who don't admit that
they watch the show.

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:40.766
- Oh!

00:01:40.766 --> 00:01:41.640
- [Kelly] Oh really?

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:43.770
- I walk through the room,
and it's on with my wife,

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.210
and I see it, but no, they're all-

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:47.070
- I don't believe in guilty pleasure.

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:48.600
I just believe in pleasure.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:49.860
I don't know why people always say-

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:51.450
- I agree.

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:52.470
- We just like it.

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:54.478
- You got that right.
Pleasure is pleasure.

00:01:54.478 --> 00:01:55.311
- What's wrong with just liking it.

00:01:55.311 --> 00:01:57.176
- And it's a character
study. You know what I mean?

00:01:57.176 --> 00:01:59.220
When you can look at it like
that, like, it's behavior

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:00.480
of these people.

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:02.400
It's like, and I know a lot of it setup,

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:03.941
but how long has she done it for?

00:02:03.941 --> 00:02:05.790
- She did it for 8 years. Now she's off.

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:09.210
And I have a degree in
psychology, and uh, I was able to-

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:10.138
- [Rose] Oh, what do you think?

00:02:10.138 --> 00:02:11.460
- [Kelly] Do you really?

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:12.789
- I do, from Yale.

00:02:12.789 --> 00:02:13.800
- What!

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:14.633
- I do.

00:02:14.633 --> 00:02:15.466
(audience laughing)

00:02:15.466 --> 00:02:18.270
- Cause you also wanted to be
an architect, I know. Right?

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:21.060
- Well originally, when
I left high school,

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:21.960
that's what I wanted to do.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:25.890
But I got kinda sidetracked,
uh, by a hell's angel

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:29.370
in some tree houses, in
La Honda, California.

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:31.252
- Did Snoop give you a blunt too?

00:02:31.252 --> 00:02:32.460
(audience laughing)

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:33.743
- It was more than a blunt.

00:02:33.743 --> 00:02:35.880
(Rose and Kelly laughing)

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:39.810
Anyway, I got sidetracked
and I missed my registration

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:41.610
to the architecture school.

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:43.800
I only had 45 minutes to register,

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:46.260
I was going to have to wait a
whole quarter to re-register

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:47.947
and the guy at the
architecture school said,

00:02:47.947 --> 00:02:50.250
"You know the drama department
is right over there,

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:52.380
and if you run over there
now, fill out the forms,

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:54.360
you might be able to get
it in under the wire."

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:55.193
- That worked out.

00:02:55.193 --> 00:02:57.720
- Yeah, how about that.
I never looked back.

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:00.030
- I love the love of
architecture. I do too.

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:02.790
I think it's so interesting
how people's minds work and-

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:05.550
- And I still am into
it, I love architecture.

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:08.160
I built a house, and I also
built a couple retail stores,

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:10.810
so I got a little bit
of it out of my blood.

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:13.200
- Well, how about the psychology
degree, did that work out?

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:14.033
How are you using that? (laughs)

00:03:14.033 --> 00:03:16.303
- Well I use that to help
Lisa get through that show.

00:03:16.303 --> 00:03:19.170
(Rose and audience laughing)

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:21.960
- What would you do if you weren't acting?

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:23.372
What do you think you would have done?

00:03:23.372 --> 00:03:25.140
- I would've done, like,
teaching or something.

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:26.340
Like a total acting- cliche.

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:27.960
I started so young, yeah I think teaching.

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:29.730
I probably would've ended up
doing something like that.

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:31.560
- That means you can be patient.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:34.778
- Well, yeah, I'm not bad.
I'm not bad until I snap.

00:03:34.778 --> 00:03:36.224
And then I'm- (laughs)

00:03:36.224 --> 00:03:37.946
- We're all not bad until we snap.

00:03:37.946 --> 00:03:40.950
- Exactly. I don't think I'm
any exception to that rule.

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:43.110
But I think, yeah. What about you Kelly?

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:45.840
- Not a teacher. Like,
no, my mom was a teacher

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:49.950
and those people are angels. I could never

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:51.780
ever do that. Like, it just takes so-

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:53.610
there's so many kids in one spot,

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:55.440
and you're wrangling them,
and they all learn differently

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:59.010
at different paces. That is
an incredibly difficult job.

00:03:59.010 --> 00:03:59.843
- Yeah.

00:03:59.843 --> 00:04:01.921
- I don't think I would've set
myself up for that, mentally.

00:04:01.921 --> 00:04:02.783
- But they're all heroes.

00:04:02.783 --> 00:04:05.820
- They're heroes, yeah,
absolutely. My mom's an incredible,

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:06.900
like, teacher.

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:08.850
I love them. I lift them up
all the time on this show,

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:10.380
but I could never. I would never-

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:11.730
- What do you think you would've done?

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:15.360
- I don't know. Like, I was
a really solid waitress,

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:16.271
I will be honest with you.

00:04:16.271 --> 00:04:17.104
(Rose and audience laughing)

00:04:17.104 --> 00:04:18.480
I know we're all in the business-

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:19.380
- Chuck E. Cheese.

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:22.623
- I would've nailed that
doll at Chuck E. Cheese, man.

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:26.370
No, I don't know. I don't
really have any- I don't know.

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:28.110
There was no other option
other than singing.

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:29.448
- I get it.

00:04:29.448 --> 00:04:31.500
- But you're in the new
movie, "80 for Brady".

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:32.493
Love the movie.

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:36.300
You play a legendary N-F-L
player, but you're in this movie,

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:38.520
also, with these iconic women. Like,

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:40.560
what was that like, being on set?

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:42.090
Because we had them all here

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:43.920
and they are a handful in the best way.

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:46.650
- I mean, how lucky was I,
to be working with those-

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:50.356
How lucky was I to kiss Jane
Fonda, in a broom closet?

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:52.626
- It's like every- In a broom
closet's my favorite part.

00:04:52.626 --> 00:04:53.700
(Harry and audience laughing)

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:56.400
And it was amazing how you got caught.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:57.870
No, but, how was it on set?

00:04:57.870 --> 00:05:00.210
I just feel like it was probably
a fun set, with everyone.

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:02.970
- It was a really fun set,
but really professional also.

00:05:02.970 --> 00:05:03.960
I mean, this is like,

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:07.980
these women are like
very very fine-aged wine.

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:11.310
And working with them was
unbelievably great, I mean,

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:14.362
and Jane Fonda, she loves to run lines.

00:05:14.362 --> 00:05:18.063
Which I like to do, too, as a
professional actor, but Rita-

00:05:18.063 --> 00:05:19.800
- What does that mean, when
you're saying running lines?

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:20.910
You mean like just-

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:23.280
- Running lines is when
you, before your scene,

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:25.410
you rehearse the scene before you go on.

00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:26.610
- Do people not do that?

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:29.370
- A lot of people don't do
that. Yeah, a lot of people-

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:31.290
- I didn't do that with Snoop.

00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:32.985
- You didn't do that with Snoop?

00:05:32.985 --> 00:05:35.250
He was like, "Let's
just wing it." (laughs)

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:36.630
- Laid back.

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:38.130
- I didn't know that. I didn't
know people didn't, like,

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:40.787
rehearse. That seems
like a- not a good idea.

00:05:40.787 --> 00:05:43.740
- It is not a good idea, that's
why professionals do that,

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:47.967
and one day Rita, um, you know,
Moreno, who's 91 by the way,

00:05:47.967 --> 00:05:49.890
and a firecracker.

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:51.981
- And does not appear 91.

00:05:51.981 --> 00:05:54.600
- Not at all. Not at all.
So there was a big scene

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:55.860
that she had coming up, but I thought-

00:05:55.860 --> 00:05:57.660
I asked her if she wanted
to run lines, you know,

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:59.700
and rehearse the scene and
she said, "Sure, let's do it."

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:02.070
So I'm reading off of the script,

00:06:02.070 --> 00:06:03.780
and I'm stumbling over the words,

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:06.060
and she has it like, (finger
snapping) 91 years old.

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:08.250
Not one single stumble all the way down.

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:09.870
- I don't know she's doing, yeah-

00:06:09.870 --> 00:06:11.481
- Whatever she's doing, we gotta do it.

00:06:11.481 --> 00:06:12.314
- Yeah, can we get that info?

00:06:12.314 --> 00:06:14.280
- It was not normal.
We all talked about it

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:15.277
when they all left. I was like,

00:06:15.277 --> 00:06:17.190
"Can we talk about how
she's supposed to be 91,

00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:18.215
like, and that' a lie?"

00:06:18.215 --> 00:06:19.048
(Harry and Rose laughing)

00:06:19.048 --> 00:06:21.420
It's like, there's no
way. Anyway, how was it

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:23.310
playing like an N-F-L
legend, that whole character?

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:24.540
Was that kind of fun?

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:26.500
- It was a blast to play but, you know,

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:27.720
(stammers)

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:30.300
I'm an actor, look, these
guys are giants, you know,

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:33.360
these football players. They're
all like seven feet tall.

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:35.130
I'm a normal human. I'm a mortal

00:06:35.130 --> 00:06:36.450
(Kelly and Rose laughing)

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:38.100
- I'm one of the mortals, not the gods.

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:40.920
- They gave me these two huge
Super Bowl rings to wear,

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:44.040
and they had to wrap the
inside of them with tape

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:46.702
because they would fall off
of my tine hands, you know.

00:06:46.702 --> 00:06:47.535
(audience laughing)

00:06:47.535 --> 00:06:48.972
I mean, these guys are gigantic.

00:06:48.972 --> 00:06:50.001
- Big dudes, yeah.

00:06:50.001 --> 00:06:51.930
- They're big, I mean, I
met Tom last night, Brady,

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:53.797
and yeah... yeah.

00:06:53.797 --> 00:06:55.890
"Hey Tom, how are you? Nice
to meet you." (chuckles)

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:59.010
- That's a good one to
meet, he's the goat, yup.

00:06:59.010 --> 00:07:00.810
Well, everybody, you
can see "80 for Brady"

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:02.947
in theaters right now, and
you can also watch Harry in

00:07:02.947 --> 00:07:04.980
"Mayfair Witches" on A-M-C.

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:06.680
Be sure to check that out as well.

